MCSKIP MT,<>
MCDEF NUMBER NL AS <MCSET S20=2
>
MCDEF PLAIN NL AS <MCSET S20=1
>
MCDEF QUIET NL AS <MCSET S20=0
>
S20 says what the listing file is to receive. It starts at zero, so
this text reaches the output and nothing else.
NUMBER
A value of two asks for the number of each output line in front of it.

The empty line above is a line like any other, and is numbered too.
PLAIN
A value of one asks for the same text without the numbers.
QUIET
Back to zero, and this line is in the output alone.
NUMBER
The count is of output lines, not of listed ones, so it has gone on
while the listing was switched off.
